# ZStats T6 settings
# Generated by tools/generate_settings.py from src/settings.json. Do not edit.
# name|type|default|section|description
zs_hud_enabled|bool|1|hud|[LIVE] Show the compact ZStats HUD. OFF hides every live row but keeps match tracking and recaps active.
zs_hud_position|enum|top_right|hud|[LIVE] Anchor the stats card to a screen corner. TOP RIGHT matches the default BO3-style layout.
zs_hud_scale|int|100|hud|[LIVE] Scale the HUD text and card. Smaller values leave more room for map-authored HUD elements.
zs_hud_preset|enum|compact|hud|[LIVE] Choose MINIMAL for time and zombies, COMPACT for the default four rows, DETAILED for every row, or CUSTOM to use the individual row toggles below.
zs_scoreboard_hud_preset|enum|detailed|hud|[LIVE] Choose the ZStats panel while viewing the in-game scoreboard. SAME uses your normal HUD preset; OFF hides the panel only during the scoreboard.
zs_hud_opacity|int|22|hud|[LIVE] Set the live HUD card background opacity. ZERO keeps the text and orange accent while removing the dark panel.
zs_hud_header|bool|1|hud|[LIVE] Show the orange ZSTATS title. OFF removes the title and collapses the extra header spacing.
zs_hud_time|bool|1|hud|[LIVE] In CUSTOM preset, show elapsed time since gameplay began for the current match.
zs_hud_zombies_left|bool|1|hud|[LIVE] In CUSTOM preset, show active AI plus the stock round spawn queue. Between rounds the HUD shows a dash instead of a misleading count.
zs_hud_ppr|bool|1|hud|[LIVE] In CUSTOM preset, show gross points earned divided by rounds observed since this player joined. This is abbreviated PPR.
zs_hud_kpr|bool|1|hud|[LIVE] In CUSTOM preset, show kills divided by rounds observed since this player joined. This is abbreviated KPR.
zs_hud_round_time|bool|0|hud|[LIVE] In CUSTOM preset, show elapsed time in the current round. Uses an observed stock round start or a valid stock round-start anchor after a late attach.
zs_hud_score|bool|0|hud|[LIVE] In CUSTOM preset, show gross positive score earned since this player joined, including the initialized starting balance. This remains distinct from spendable points and shows a Career PB after exceeding the saved best match total.
zs_hud_round_kills|bool|0|hud|[LIVE] In CUSTOM preset, show kills gained during the current round and mark a new personal best using the selected PB scope.
zs_hud_round_points|bool|0|hud|[LIVE] In CUSTOM preset, show gross points earned during the current round and mark a new personal best using the selected PB scope.
zs_hud_headshots|bool|0|hud|[LIVE] In CUSTOM preset, show headshot kills gained during the current round and mark a new personal best using the selected PB scope.
zs_hud_round_revives|bool|0|hud|[LIVE] In CUSTOM preset, show revives made during the current round and mark a new personal best using the selected PB scope. Solo displays N/A.
zs_hud_round_number|bool|0|hud|[LIVE] In CUSTOM preset, show the current stock round number as its own aligned row. Career mode marks a new highest round.
zs_hud_personal_best|bool|1|hud|[LIVE] Mark KPR/PPR and completed-round kill, point, headshot, melee, and revive records; Career mode also marks new best match earnings, match kills, and highest round.
zs_pb_scope|enum|career|recap|[NEXT MATCH] CAREER compares against this client's saved Zombies records across matches. MATCH ONLY resets personal-best comparisons when a new match begins.
zs_pb_round_announce|bool|1|recap|[NEXT ROUND END] Show a concise client-only message when a completed round sets one or more personal bests. This is separate from the shared Round MVP announcement.
zs_round_report|bool|1|recap|[NEXT ROUND END] Post one round MVP callout in the game feed, including the category in which that player led the team.
zs_game_over_report|bool|1|recap|[NEXT GAME OVER] Show a paginated ZStats recap after the stock scoreboard: personal summary and records in solo, or team awards plus the local player's summary in co-op.
zs_show_lowlights|bool|0|recap|[NEXT GAME OVER] Add a light-hearted Most Downs line to the game-over panel. OFF keeps the default recap entirely positive.
zs_recap_seconds|int|20|recap|[NEXT GAME OVER] Total seconds allocated across the ZStats game-over recap pages. ZStats reserves enough time on stock-compatible intermission flows; custom endings may not honor the reservation.
